  "title": "A COVID-19 survivors and close contacts EEG dataset",
  "description": "This dataset comprises resting-state EEG recordings from 173 individuals, including 86 healthy close contacts and 87 COVID-19 survivors, collected at the Cuban Neuroscience Center. The dataset was designed to characterize EEG signatures associated with COVID-19 survival and to compare them with a Cuban EEG normative database. Recordings were obtained using a standard 10-20 montage under resting conditions with eyes closed and alternating eyes open/closed periods.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was acquired using a 10-20 standard montage. Resting EEG was recorded for 8 minutes with eyes closed, followed by 2 minutes alternating between eyes closed and eyes open, and a final 2-minute recovery period.",
